{"schema":"fstar-module-docs","version":2,"module":"DocsSugar","interface":false,"declarations":[{"name":"DocsSugar.double","kind":"let","signature":"x: Prims.int -> Prims.int","range":{"file":"DocsSugar.fst","start_line":19,"start_col":0,"end_line":19,"end_col":32},"doc":["Doubles 'x'."]},{"name":"DocsSugar.triple","kind":"let","signature":"x: Prims.int -> Prims.int","range":{"file":"DocsSugar.fst","start_line":30,"start_col":0,"end_line":30,"end_col":32},"doc":["Triples 'x'.","","Continuation lines are dedented by their common indentation, so this","paragraph sits flush with the first line rather than keeping the","four spaces it is written with.","","A leading `*` would be part of the text rather than stripped: the","payload is opaque, and deciding what a `*` means would be","interpreting it."]},{"name":"DocsSugar.attributed","kind":"let","signature":"x: Prims.int -> Prims.int","range":{"file":"DocsSugar.fst","start_line":43,"start_col":0,"end_line":43,"end_col":32},"doc":["Documented and attributed at once. The doc comment desugars to its","own attribute set, so before `add_decorations` learned to","concatenate them this was rejected as \"more than one attribute set\".","Around a hundred declarations in `ulib` are written this way."]},{"name":"DocsSugar.nested","kind":"let","signature":"x: Prims.int -> Prims.int","range":{"file":"DocsSugar.fst","start_line":47,"start_col":0,"end_line":47,"end_col":28},"doc":["A nested (* comment *) is part of the documentation text, not the","end of it."]},{"name":"DocsSugar.empty_comment_still_works","kind":"let","signature":"x: Prims.int -> Prims.int","range":{"file":"DocsSugar.fst","start_line":51,"start_col":0,"end_line":52,"end_col":12},"doc":["The empty-comment idiom still lexes as `(*` followed by `*)`, so it","is a comment in expression position and not a marker."]},{"name":"DocsSugar.flag","kind":"type","signature":"Type0","range":{"file":"DocsSugar.fst","start_line":56,"start_col":5,"end_line":56,"end_col":9},"doc":["A tiny type. As for a hand-written attribute, this documents","`flag` and neither `On` nor `Off`."]}]}
